  deathsLabel:n=>n?`Recorded deaths (${n.toLocaleString('en-US')} records missing this value)`:'Recorded deaths',
  abs:(o)=>`Landslides kill thousands of people every year, and ${o.rain}% of the ${o.total} records in the local Global Landslide Catalog file were classified as rain-triggered. Data Detectives turns NASA POWER daily series (1981–present; the product varies by period) into extreme-rainfall and soil-wetness indices, tests whether those indices are changing (Mann-Kendall and Sen’s slope), and measures their historical response to El Niño and La Niña (NOAA ONI). Two gradient boosting models complete the analysis: one produces a score of similarity to conditions on recorded landslide days (AUC ${o.auc1} at places excluded from training), and the other was validated for recurrence of records in historical years after its training period (AUC ${o.auc2}). The latest ONI in the file is ${o.oni} °C in ${o.seas} (${o.cur}); it is not a real-time reading.`,
